[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65491,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 234,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Florid reactive lymphoid hyperplasia is a dense, atypical-appearing lymphoid infiltrate simulating lymphoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:06:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65492,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 234,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:06:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65493,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 234,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:06:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65494,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 234,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> pseudolymphoma; lymphoma-like lesion</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:06:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65495,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 234,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:06:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65496,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 234,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These lesions occur most commonly in the cervix, less often in the endometrium, and rarely in the vulva.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:06:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65497,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 234,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Reactive lymphoid hyperplasia almost always occurs in premenopausal woman; it may present with vaginal or postcoital bleeding or may be an incidental finding discovered during work-up of squamous dysplasia {4086158; 17413989}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:06:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65498,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 234,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The epidemiology is unknown.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:06:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65499,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 234,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Florid reactive lymphoid hyperplasia may occur in the setting of infection (EBV, <em>Chlamydia trachomatis</em>, HIV, or HPV), with use of intrauterine devices, and after surgical procedures {20087162; 22056039}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:06:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65500,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 234,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesion is a reactive inflammatory process.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:06:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65501,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 234,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The cervix may be eroded and friable, but the lesions are usually superficial, and large masses are very uncommon.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:06:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65502,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 234,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Reactive lymphoid hyperplasia is superficially located, with or without ulceration, and extends only a few millimetres into the wall. It is composed of a polymorphous infiltrate of large and small lymphoid cells including immunoblasts, with admixed plasma cells and neutrophils. The appearance may be worrisome (suggestive of lymphoma), but the superficial distribution is reassuring. Immunostaining reveals a mixture of B&nbsp;cells, T&nbsp;cells, and polytypic plasma cells. A background of more-typical chronic cervicitis or endometritis is often present. The lesions may show clonal IGH rearrangements, but this does not indicate lymphoma, and patients remain disease-free on follow-up {20087162}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:06:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65503,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 234,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is a polymorphous inflammatory infiltrate.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:06:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65504,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 234,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:06:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65505,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 234,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> superficial distribution; lack of sclerosis; no evidence of a mass lesion; a polymorphous lymphoid infiltrate.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:06:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65506,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 234,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:06:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65507,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 234,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This is a benign lesion.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:06:29"
      }
    ],
